  "body": "The [`autocomplete` attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#autofill) for credit card attributes currently supports `cc-exp`, `cc-exp-month` and `cc-exp-year`.\r\n\r\nThis has a couple of issues:\r\n\r\n`cc-exp` is described as a expiration time expressed in `YYYY-MM` format. All credit cards that I have seen so far print the expiration time in `MM/YY` format on the cards. This is also what websites ask for quite frequently.\r\n\r\n`cc-exp-year` is described as the expiration year expressed in `YYYY` format. As stated above, all credit cards that I have seen use the `YY` format for the expiration year. This is also common on websites.\r\n\r\nShould we introduce for example `cc-exp-mmyy` and `cc-exp-year-yy`?",
